cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Sebel Hakim, its trained model or its disease knowledge base, please cite it as below.
  Please also cite the datasets listed under "references": the model was trained on their images.
type: software
title: "Sebel Hakim: free, offline AI diagnosis of crop diseases for African farmers"
abstract: >-
  Sebel Hakim (Amharic: "crop doctor") is a free progressive web app that identifies the plant and the most likely
  disease or pest from a photo of a leaf and gives management advice in integrated-pest-management order (farm
  practices, then biological options, then chemicals as a last resort). The AI model (EfficientNet-B0 distilled from
  a ConvNeXt-V2 teacher, 108 classes across 23 crops) runs on the phone with ONNX Runtime Web, so the app works
  offline and photos never leave the device. Model v2 was trained on 136,735 images from 12 public datasets and
  reaches 93.9% top-1 accuracy on 13,676 held-out test images (90.3% on field photos). The interface is available
  in English, Amharic, French, Swahili and Italian.
